  "lineage": "Songs of Saint Lucia's two rival flower societies, La Woz (La Rose) and La Magwit (La Marguerite), each organised as a mock royal court of kings, queens and other officers. Members meet in weekly séances to sing their society's Kwéyòl songs, led by a chantwèl, and celebrate their patron saints' feasts, 30 August for La Rose and 17 October for La Marguerite, with mass, a costumed procession and a feast; the shaker card stands in for the chak-chak rattle.",
